-- title:
--   Conditional expectation of every integrable functional of a countably sampled future Lévy path
-- statement:
--   Fix a spectrally negative Lévy process X, past time s and an arbitrary countable future observation schedule τ. Suppose the joint sigma algebra generated by the first n future increment observations X_(s+τ_i)−X_s is independent of F_s for EVERY finite prefix n. Then for any Borel measurable real functional f on the complete sampled future path (Nat→Real), provided f(sampled future path) is integrable, its conditional expectation given F_s equals its constant unconditional expectation almost surely. This includes bounded indicators of measurable future-path survival and arbitrary integrable path-dependent future rewards. It follows from the newly officially accepted full countable sampled-path independence theorem, sigma algebra containment under composition with f and pinned Mathlib condExp_indep_eq. The remaining actual Lévy application must establish the uniform finite-prefix independence from the original full-filtration independent increments. No unjustified independence of individual coordinates is assumed.
-- source:
--   ACCEPTED chat04_shifted_countable_path_independent_of_all_finite_prefixes UUID 42f8ec77-38ce-4b1d-a188-33f6193cea0e, ACCEPTED chat04_general_future_increment_conditional_expectation as proof pattern UUID 60e3f274-5580-448a-a1d8-6485fa8ab41a, pinned Mathlib condExp_indep_eq.

